n-we-thought/'}, {'signal_id': '1b6780d40e17f368', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Would NATO Membership for Ukraine Undermine Article 5 Itself? <p>In 2025, Jennifer Kavanaugh and Christopher McCallion wrote, &#8220;Armed Neutrality for Ukraine Is NATO&#8217;s Least Poor Option,&#8221; where they made the case for armed neutrality over full NATO membership as t', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/would-nato-membership-for-ukraine-undermine-article-5-itself/'}, {'signal_id': 'ba38c72ae33bc53d', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Strategic Stability and the Rebuilding of Xi’s Military <p>For all the warnings about an increasingly capable Chinese military, this may very well be an awkward moment for Beijing to have that military tested. General Secretary Xi Jinping has hollowed out much of the People&#8217', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/strategic-stability-and-the-rebuilding-of-xis-military/'}, {'signal_id': '0e3e84200aea153a', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Three Patrons, Three Clients: The Mecca Alliance No One Owns <p>Every alliance contains a struggle over who gets to decide what the alliance is for. The unusual thing about the Mecca Alliance, formally known as the &#8220;Mecca Joint Defence Agreement,&#8221; is that all three of', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/three-patrons-three-clients-the-mecca-alliance-no-one-owns/'}, {'signal_id': '60d56685c2a1dbaa', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Reading the Kremlin’s Mind: Ukrainian Writers Attempt to Understand Putin <p>Welcome to&#160;The Ukraine Compass, a weekly digest of Ukrainian commentary and analysis from across the political spectrum, only for War on the Rocks&#160;members. Each Monday, we bring you a curated s', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/reading-the-kremlins-mind-ukrainian-writers-attempt-to-understand-putin/'}, {'signal_id': '5321bc66169b0448', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'This Is Not Your Father’s Nuclear Flight Test Vehicle <p>For decades, the United States&#8217; nuclear weapons enterprise has wrestled with an institutional paradox. On one hand is the imperative to make the complex more &#8220;responsive&#8221; to global tumult and technical sur', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/this-is-not-your-fathers-nuclear-flight-test-vehicle/'}, {'signal_id': '144f18951d48a536', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Big Bet on the Emerging Space Economy <p>The space economy has surpassed $600 billion in annual value, with some projecting it will reach a trillion by the 2030s. Jonathan Panter is joined by Joseph Yaffe (Cowboy Space), Brian Weeden (The Aerospace Corporation), and Dan Wald ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/the-big-bet-on-the-emerging-space-economy/'}, {'signal_id': '572beec097ba7921', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Age of Strategic Exclusion <p>Major powers are increasingly trying to shut out their rivals. Russia invaded Ukraine in part to prevent the latter&#8217;s further integration with the West. The United States is restricting China&#8217;s access to advanced semiconductors and en', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-age-of-strategic-exclusion/'}, {'signal_id': 'f0fc561dabb21987', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The War’s Last Generation Is Still Holding America’s Moral Debt <p>On the first night of the evacuation of Kabul, Aug. 15, 2021, a young mother found me in the crowd at Hamid Karzai International Airport. She had marked me, correctly, as someone who spoke her language. By the end', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-wars-last-generation-is-still-holding-americas-moral-debt/'}, {'signal_id': '4b88f91f1e94cc8a', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'What America’s Adversaries and Allies Hope to Gain at the U.N. General Assembly <p>This year&#8217;s U.N. General Assembly officially opened on Tuesday, Sept. 8. The annual gathering gives diplomats and leaders a valuable opportunity to press their foreign policy priorities and e', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/what-americas-adversaries-and-allies-hope-to-gain-at-the-u-n-general-assembly/'}, {'signal_id': 'a7390c5588471bb5', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Automating the Action Officer: Between Bureaucracy and Technology <p>If there is a revolution brewing in the automation of white-collar work, you wouldn&#8217;t know it at the Pentagon. Here, the typical action officers, staff who tackle the daily work of the bureaucracy, perform', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/automating-the-action-officer-between-bureaucracy-and-technology/'}, {'signal_id': '0b26e2a94a596635', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Assessment Gap in U.S. Counter-Terrorism Strikes <p>For eight years I helped decide whether American counter-terrorism money was working.As a programs advisor in the State Department&#8217;s Bureau of Counterterrorism from 2018 to 2025, I oversaw about 20 projects in East Afr', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-assessment-gap-in-u-s-counter-terrorism-strikes/'}, {'signal_id': '2d8abdb2b2846625', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Forced Into the Right Decision? A Look at U.S. Land-Based Deterrence Posture <p>In 2019, Steve Fetter wrote &#8220;A Cheaper Nuclear Sponge,&#8221; in which he argued that building a new intercontinental ballistic missile (ICBM) was unnecessary for strengthening U.S. land-based d', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/forced-into-the-right-decision-a-look-at-u-s-land-based-deterrence-posture/'}, {'signal_id': 'cd0808c402ea03a0', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Tyranny of Shipyard Cost-Plus Contracting <p>As a naval shipyard commander, my mandate from Navy leadership is straightforward:&#160;return warships to the fleet as quickly as possible.&#160;Neither my shipyard nor many other public and private shipyards are consistently fulf', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/the-tyranny-of-shipyard-cost-plus-contracting/'}, {'signal_id': '1fa4ef77cf82cdeb', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Strange Transformation of the Front Line in Ukraine <p>On Jan. 5, 2025, my volunteer platoon attached to the 23rd Special Purpose Battalion of the Presidential Brigade entered a 1-kilometer-long tree line called CHAI, on the outskirts of Kotlyne, a few kilometers west of Pokr', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-strange-transformation-of-the-front-line-in-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': '1670eaafeaf89241', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Mecca Pact’s Credibility Gap <p>Collective-defense pacts are meant to make war less likely. Poorly designed ones can do the opposite. If allies make sweeping promises without the military integration, decision-making mechanisms, and escalation controls needed to carry them ou', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-mecca-pacts-credibility-gap/'}, {'signal_id': '179f7c3bf766d1d7', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Two Questions Ukraine Asks Before Every Decision <p>Welcome to&#160;The Ukraine Compass, a weekly digest of Ukrainian commentary and analysis from across the political spectrum, only for War on the Rocks&#160;members. Each Monday, we bring you a curated selection of articles ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-two-questions-ukraine-asks-before-every-decision/'}, {'signal_id': '6114ee09bd6fceae', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Kids are Alright: U.S. Soft Power, Aid, and Youth in Africa <p><em>OPINION — A recent survey of African youth challenges conventional wisdom on foreign aid. Policymakers should take heed of their views as they design the future of U.S. foreign assistance to increase effective', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-kids-are-alright'}, {'signal_id': 'c6ca6333ccf272ad', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "F-35 Fallacy: Jets Alone Will Not Save Us <p>NATO Allies have bet the future of European skies on the world’s most sophisticated combat aircraft. NATO Allies are buying the world's most advanced fighter but many are neglecting vital investments in hard security, ground crews, and", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/f-35-fallacy-jets-alone-will-not-save-us'}, {'signal_id': 'fee7d3e35b4d3134', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The U.S. Military Has Much to Learn From Ukraine <p>“What does Ukraine really need? How do we make sure they're delivering what they actually need? And you know, right now those are air defense munitions, it's funding for drones, it's extended range artillery, electronic warfare,", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/why-americas-military-still-needs-its-allies'}, {'signal_id': '1a2041754d6a8495', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Terms We Must Set <p>On October 23, Russia's deputy prime minister said three tankers were at sea, that supply contracts were being finalized, and that volumes would rise to 1 million tons in December and could reach 3 million a month. A week earlier, the United States had wa", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-terms-we-must-set'}, {'signal_id': '15cbfb74f4b66b65', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Thirteenth Mile: This Is What Gray Zone War Looks Like <p>On the morning of October 23, the cargo ship Khoryv sent a distress call <a href="https://www.kyivpost.com/post/88003" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">13 nautical miles off Constanța</a>, Romania. Territorial', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-thirteenth-mile-this-is-what-gray-zone-war-looks-like'}, {'signal_id': '2bbcaebde45ce997', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Intelligence Community’s Missing Discipline <p>Economic statecraft has become a primary instrument of US national security, deployed with a frequency and ambition that outpaces the intelligence architecture built to support it. For sanctions, tariffs, investment screening, ex', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-intelligence-communitys-missing-discipline'}, {'signal_id': '535c3685a554e588', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'We’re Losing the Cognitive Space Race <p>Over the last century, modern medicine achieved a historic feat. We increased the human lifespan by 33%. But at the same time, we completely failed to defend our brain healthspan. Today, a silent gap of 15 to 30 years exists between the ti', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/were-losing-the-cognitive-space-race'}, {'signal_id': '4b15e2360fb8530e', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Russia Never Left the International Financial System. It Built a Way Back In. <p>A7’s OpenAI prompt was six words long: "Translate [name] to [language]. Answer only translated text."</p><p>Developer code leaked in 2025 from A7—the Kremlin-linked payment network designated by Trea', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/russia-never-left-the-international-financial-system-it-built-a-way-back-in'}, {'signal_id': 'fcc142ead8a66abb', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Turkey Has Outsourced Its Censorship to American Companies <p>Earlier this month, Sky News correspondent <a href="https://ground.news/article/sky-news-reporter-alex-crawfords-x-account" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Alex Crawford</a> got a notice from X: her account w', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/turkey-has-outsourced-its-censorship-to-american-companies'}, {'signal_id': 'e1b2c0d145ded66c', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Technology Is Outrunning the Way We Fight <p>The United States is racing to field AI and autonomous systems. It is not racing to figure out how to fight with them. This imbalance between technology and concepts is widening a gap the U.S. is ill prepared to close. Ukraine has show', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/technology-is-outrunning-the-way-we-fight'}, {'signal_id': '15b847110bac0873', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Hybrid Threats: Why Awareness Must Transcend Individual Cyberattacks <p>Every October, Cybersecurity Awareness Month puts practical security measures in the spotlight. Can an employee recognize a phishing email? Will someone pause before clicking a suspicious link? Are passwords ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/hybrid-threats-why-awareness-must-transcend-individual-cyberattacks'}, {'signal_id': '46024bc6e9fc668a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'America\'s Counter-Drone Authority Is Real, The Capacity Isn\'t Yet <p>Here is a number worth sitting with: federal teams seized roughly <a href="https://dronexl.co/2026/10/05/fbi-counter-drone-school-double-capacity-woodward" target="_blank" title="https://dronexl.co/2026/10/05/fb', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/america-s-counter-drone-authority-is-real-the-capacity-isn-t-yet'}, {'signal_id': '217c50e76268bc84', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The U.S. Army’s Pacific Strategy Depends on Allies <p>“We never fight alone. We've never done that. You can go all the way back to the days of Revolutionary War. The United States has never gone into conflict on its own. We've always built coalitions. We've always involved partne", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-u-s-armys-pacific-strategy-depends-on-allies'}, {'signal_id': '612051baeeba5542', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Hidden Risks of AI-Powered Intelligence <p><span>Picture an </span>intelligent analyst's screen. Data about troop movements, a port closure, a terrorist attack, or a weapons transfer sits at the center of a clean interface, with a confidence indicator glowing green. Two hundr", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-hidden-risks-of-ai-powered-intelligence'}, {'signal_id': '67fbdeb10f8d3e21', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'What a Russian Hybrid Attack Might Look Like <p>Russia has demonstrated a growing willingness to use hybrid tactics – including sabotage, cyberattacks, information operations, and the use of deniable or “throwaway” agents – to create disruption and uncertainty across Europe. This', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/what-a-russian-hybrid-attack-might-look-like'}, {'signal_id': 'aabdf5a0d915c66e', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Muhammad bin Salman’s Humbling and the Return of the Ottomans <p>The Houthis bloodied Saudi Crown Prince Muhammad bin Salman’s nose—again—with their deadly, cruel, but effective attacks on Riyadh’s King Khalid International Airport last week. The strikes are the latest in a serie', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/muhammad-bin-salmans-humbling-and-the-return-of-the-ottomans'}, {'signal_id': '1768a2a205f8c24a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Day We Cannot Choose <p>Washington made three decisions this week, and none of them has an end date. On the night of October 14, Ukrainian units in the field found that their Starshield terminals had been capped at a speed, 160 kilometers an hour by the published figure, 70 b', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-day-we-cannot-choose'}, {'signal_id': '809453e0a348c58b', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'How Far Should the U.S. Go to Defend Saudi Arabia? <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/saudi-yemen-us-israel-iran-war.jpg?id=68454050&amp;width=1245&amp;height=700&amp;coordinates=0%2C53%2C0%2C53" /><br /><br /><p><em>Recent deadly attacks by Yemen\'s Iranian-ba', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/how-far-should-the-u-s-go-to-defend-saudi-arabia'}, {'signal_id': 'b097fb4beb88b6eb', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Who Really Makes Decisions in Tehran? <p>Ayatollah Ali Khamenei’s death led to greater decentralization of the regime and a more collective, securitized decision-making system. In Iran today, authority is distributed across several actors and groups, in which the military-securit', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/who-really-makes-decisions-in-tehran'}, {'signal_id': 'd5f29eddafe9987c', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Soviet Roots of Russia’s Modern Disinformation War <p>Anti-Semitism, the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. pronounced while repudiating an anti-Israel resolution adopted at the 1967 National <a href="https://www.jta.org/archive/dr-king-repudiates-anti-semitic-anti-israel-black-', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-soviet-roots-of-russias-modern-disinformation-war'}, {'signal_id': 'e217dc903f365fe4', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Europe’s Changing Politics and the Future of U.S. Leadership <p>“And now, there is war again. There is new competition between great powers. There is vulnerability, aggression, terrorism, a whole universe of new threats and attacks again. And so, we must rebuild our institutions ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/europes-changing-politics-and-the-future-of-u-s-leadership'}, {'signal_id': 'c5b36c915fd20f4c', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'What Beijing Calls Open, Washington Should Call an Operation <p><em>China is about to run the largest influence operation in history. It will not have to run it. The world will download it.</em><em></em></p><p><strong>EXPERT PERSPECTIVE</strong> -- Our research team at Vanderbilt', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/what-beijing-calls-open-washington-should-call-an-operation-2678089778'}, {'signal_id': '2e00ae1d8820c2c2', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Washington Cannot Outsource Saudi Security to the Mecca Pact <p>The Houthis have significantly escalated their airstrike campaign targeting civilian infrastructure in Saudi Arabia, with <a href="https://apnews.com/article/saudi-yemen-houthi-riyadh-airport-d2e0868ffb18d883c16465d7', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/washington-cannot-outsource-saudi-security-to-the-mecca-pact'}, {'signal_id': '3f263fbed8d41717', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Next War of Attrition is in Yemen <p>Battlefield dynamics in Yemen shift quickly, but Houthi aims do not. A movement organized around radical ideology and perpetual conflict now shares a border with a state organized around modernization and prosperity. Saudi Arabia and the H', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-next-war-of-attrition-is-in-yemen'}, {'signal_id': '5fb5d97689873bb8', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Pentagon’s Drone Revolution Starts With Soldiers <p><strong><em>Welcome to The Iron Triangle, the Cipher Brief column serving Procurement Officers tasked with buying the future, Investors funding the next generation of defense technology, and the Policy Wonks analyzing its im', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-pentagons-drone-revolution-starts-with-soldiers'}, {'signal_id': 'a8bfe1115b4e57c4', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'America’s Military Has a GPS Problem <p>“The Department of Defense’s (DoD) Global Positioning System (GPS) is the principal source of positioning, navigation, and timing (PNT) information for the U.S. military and civilian users. Due to DoD’s reliance on it, GPS also represents a', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/americas-military-has-a-gps-problem'}, {'signal_id': '42be15b3b1569d3d', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Subterranean Warfare - An Urgent DoW Need Without An Owner <p>The DoW urgently needs to organize its scattered subterranean warfare assets into a single unified organization. Ideally, a Direct Reporting Portfolio Manager (DRPM) for Subterranean Warfare, reporting to the Deputy Se', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/subterranean-warfare-an-urgent-dow-need-without-an-owner'}, {'signal_id': 'f8f75a5bf7797164', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Sanctions We Cannot Afford <p>On the evening of Friday, October 9, the Treasury published General License 135. It authorizes the “sale, delivery, offloading and importation” of Russian diesel until April 7, 2027, and does not specify a buyer, a seller, or a quantity. The Pres', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-sanctions-we-cannot-afford'}, {'signal_id': '5bdf089f2b16dd6d', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'How Ukraine’s Ground Robots Are Changing the Battlefield <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/the-214th-separate-assault-battalion-opfor-training-held-in-ukraine.jpg?id=68398449&amp;width=1245&amp;height=700&amp;coordinates=0%2C53%2C0%2C54" /><br /><br /><p><em>', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/how-ukraines-ground-robots-are-changing-the-battlefield'}, {'signal_id': 'bf9e12e84d1dc0b3', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Next Drone Won't Have a Radio Link, Our Intelligence Enterprise Needs to Plan for That Now <p>On the last day of the 2026 World Cup, NORAD F-16s fired flares over northern New Jersey to warn off civilian pilots who had flown into restricted airspace. During the tournament, fe", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-next-drone-won-t-have-a-radio-link-our-intelligence-enterprise-needs-to-plan-for-that-now'}, {'signal_id': '7ff27e75e87e2619', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Just the Docs: Federal Judge Rejects DOJ Bid to Sequester 20,000 California Mail Ballots <p>Order: Federal judge denies DOJ request to make California set aside 20,000 mail ballots from alleged noncitizens.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/162670/judge-carter', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162670/judge-carter-denies-doj-california-ballots-tro/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=judge-carter-denies-doj-california-ballots-tro'}, {'signal_id': '36104d0d2aa3425d', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'The “Presumption of Regularity” in Trump Administration Litigation (5th edition) <p>The most comprehensive study of court cases involving the Trump administration from January 20, 2025 to present</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/120547/presumption-of-regulari', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/120547/presumption-of-regularity/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=presumption-of-regularity'}, {'signal_id': '1bb31ce66a481838', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Liability Could Rein In Rogue AI Agents. Current Law Falls Short. <p>The three changes that would make AI companies answer for the conduct of their systems and catastrophic risks. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/162331/liability-rein-in-rogue-ai-agents/">Li', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162331/liability-rein-in-rogue-ai-agents/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=liability-rein-in-rogue-ai-agents'}, {'signal_id': '3fff40356d70ee07', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Early Edition: October 30, 2026 <p>Sign up to receive the Early Edition in your inbox\xa0here. A curated weekday guide to major news and developments over the last 24 hours. Here’s today’s news: IRAN WAR U.S. Central Command Cdr. Adm. Brad Cooper yesterday briefed President Trump in', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162627/early-edition-october-30-2026/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=early-edition-october-30-2026'}, {'signal_id': '1197de37ef1e5e9d', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Guantanamo Dispatches: USS Cole Defense Lawyers Make 11th Hour Plea for Delay of Trial Starting Monday <p>With jury selection set to begin in just a few days, the senior military defense lawyer in the USS Cole bombing case asked the judge to postpone the trial by six months.</p>\n', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162545/uss-cole-trial-defense-plea-delay/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=uss-cole-trial-defense-plea-delay'}, {'signal_id': '238a03eb0a27be99', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Just the Docs: Unsealed Criminal Information Against James Comey Under Espionage Act <p>Unsealed criminal information charges ex-FBI Director James Comey under the Espionage Act over alleged 2016 leak.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/162425/comey-espionage-a', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162425/comey-espionage-act-information/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=comey-espionage-act-information'}, {'signal_id': 'f8c4fc2faf667424', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Why is the Government Hiding Court Rebuke on Warrantless FISA Surveillance? <p>Government agencies have been misusing FISA 702 and the Trump administration is now breaking the law to hide this misconduct from the public.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/16045', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/160451/government-hiding-rebuke-warrantless-fisa-surveillance/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=government-hiding-rebuke-warrantless-fisa-surveillance'}, {'signal_id': '706dcb9137e65c5d', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Data Centers as Military Objectives: The Russian and Ukrainian Justifications <p>Experts examine four major international legal questions raised by Russian and Ukrainian attacks on data centers.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/162054/data-centers-military-ob', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162054/data-centers-military-objectives-russia-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=data-centers-military-objectives-russia-ukraine'}, {'signal_id': '214359e5804a1f1e', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'What Leaders Can do Now and Next to Lower Risks of Election Violence <p>Congress could take several obvious steps to make it safer to participate in the American democratic system.\xa0</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/162186/leaders-do-lower-risk-election-violen', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162186/leaders-do-lower-risk-election-violence/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=leaders-do-lower-risk-election-violence'}, {'signal_id': '16ea0fdfc5b1ca35', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Early Edition: October 29, 2026 <p>Sign up to receive the Early Edition in your inbox\xa0here. A curated weekday guide to major news and developments over the last 24 hours. Here’s today’s news: IRAN WAR U.S. Vice President JD Vance sent a letter to Iranian Secretary of the Supreme ', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162389/early-edition-october-29-2026/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=early-edition-october-29-2026'}, {'signal_id': '27c968e09255c3ca', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "America's Least Bad Option in Iran In Iran, the United States could return to a full-scale bombing campaign, walk away from the conflict, or stick with the current approach. Staying the course almost certainly will not bring quick results but it is strategically prudent.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/americas-least-bad-option-in-iran.html'}, {'signal_id': '1360f15fbaf3d074', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Why Quick Compensation Hasn't Replaced Eaton Fire Lawsuits—So Far A review of Southern California Edison's direct-payment program finds that it has paid claimants much faster, but it hasn't become a broad substitute for lawsuits.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/why-quick-compensation-hasnt-replaced-eaton-fire-lawsuits.html'}, {'signal_id': 'b8e2180ad066e052', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The Missing Link in Drug Policy: Why Whole-System Reform Is Stalling The UK has made progress toward a whole-system approach to drug policy, but unclear accountability and persistent stigma are stalling reform.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/the-missing-link-in-drug-policy-why-whole-system-reform.html'}, {'signal_id': '1c27b342495b14b7', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "A Better Way to Use Criminal Records in Hiring Employers want to know whether an applicant is likely to commit another crime, possibly on the job. But the screening rules many of them use are often about as accurate as a coin toss, in part because they're based on data that don't", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/a-better-way-to-use-criminal-records-in-hiring.html'}, {'signal_id': '1f82f8da9de912b0', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Biosecurity in the Age of AI: Q&amp;A with Steph Guerra The question that drives Steph Guerra's work at RAND may be one of the most consequential for this moment in the AI era: How can we harness the full potential of AI for science and medicine—but also ensure it never helps any", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/biosecurity-in-the-age-of-ai-qa-with-steph-guerra.html'}, {'signal_id': '510596eafa31042f', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'From Strategic Logic to Practical Implementation: A Phased Agenda for U.S.-ROK Shipbuilding Cooperation U.S.-ROK cooperation on shipbuilding should be structured so that it strengthens U.S. maritime industrial capacity, makes commercial sense for Korean shipbuilders, and survives', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/from-strategic-logic-to-practical-implementation-a.html'}, {'signal_id': 'c5904b48ce512115', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "9/11's Forgotten Lesson Twenty-five years later, 9/11's lessons are still contested, except the simplest: the United States mistook quiet for peace. And it is doing so again.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/911s-forgotten-lesson.html'}, {'signal_id': '645e5c8159c45b3c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Schools, Cell Phones, and AI: Q&amp;A with Melissa Kay Diliberti Melissa Kay Diliberti, an associate policy researcher at RAND, discusses recent findings from RAND that can help parents and policymakers better understand what challenges schools are up against.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/schools-cell-phones-and-ai-qa-with-melissa-kay-diliberti.html'}, {'signal_id': 'f0a6bf01926bc40a', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Netanyahu May Have Ignored a Dire Warning. Israel Ignores the Deeper Threat. Israel's strategy in Gaza is only keeping Hamas in power: deterred, but not replaced, with no real alternative given a chance. A different outcome calls for a different approach.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/nentanyahu-may-have-ignored-a-dire-warning-israel-ignores-the.html'}, {'signal_id': 'b489a15858be84c1', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Never Underestimate the Houthis Yemen's Houthi rebels are in a position to shape the next phase of the conflict between the United States and Iran if they attempt to renew their blockade of the Bab al-Mandab Strait. And no one should assume that a deal with Iran will bind what th", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/never-underestimate-the-houthis.html'}, {'signal_id': '19d8064c433770cf', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Preserving Jobs and Tax Revenue in the Age of AI: Q&amp;A with Carter Price Carter Price, a mathematician at RAND and co-director of the RAND Von Furstenberg Family Budget Model Initiative, discusses ways to rebalance the tax code so that it doesn't incentivize employers to repla", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/preserving-jobs-and-tax-revenue-in-the-age-of-ai-qa.html'}, {'signal_id': 'd2d02311d1d9e0e7', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The Recent Rise of Women Gun Owners In recent years, women made up almost half of all new gun owners, a striking shift from the historical norm, when women accounted for about a quarter of them. And the uptick is widespread across geographic and demographic subgroups.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/the-recent-rise-of-women-gun-owners.html'}, {'signal_id': '2a9dc8988cf7146c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Who Benefits from Education Savings Accounts? Q&amp;A with Susha Roy Tens of thousands of American families use state-funded education savings accounts for their children's education. How exactly do these accounts work? Who benefits from them? And how do they affect education fun", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/who-benefits-from-education-savings-accounts.html'}, {'signal_id': '480b7da85115059d', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Getting a Security Clearance Doesn't Have to Be So Intimidating: Q&amp;A with Sina Beaghley The security clearance process can be difficult and time-consuming but the government has made big strides in improving it. Sina Beaghley, a senior international and defense researcher at ", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/getting-a-security-clearance-doesnt-have-to-be-so-intimidating.html'}, {'signal_id': 'd2b8719ed5ca0a96', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': '25 Years After 9/11: Lessons for Securing the Homeland Reflecting on 25 years since the September 11 terror attacks, RAND experts answer questions about protecting soft targets, the role of the TSA, mitigating risks from emerging technologies, and more.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/25-years-after-911-lessons-for-securing-the-homeland.html'}, {'signal_id': '080553cfaf2bb84f', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'AI Can Now Design Viruses. We Need Biosecurity Guardrails Now As AI advances, the risk of engineered viral bioweapons is growing. The window to prepare is now—by building a layered, resilient system of defense.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/ai-can-now-design-viruses-we-need-biosecurity-guardrails.html'}, {'signal_id': '20bc7f624125f201', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Tomorrow's Victory and the Army of the Future: Forecasting the Next Steps in Ukraine's Military Evolution Ukraine’s military has changed substantially since Russia’s full-scale invasion in 2022. Will its next evolution be shaped by traditionalists or technologists?", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/tomorrows-victory-and-the-army-of-the-future.html'}, {'signal_id': 'f540d78c60af3817', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'When Disaster Strikes, Could AI Help? Q&amp;A with Jessica Jensen Disasters are more frequent, more severe, and more costly. Pressure is mounting on emergency managers and the organizations that support them. Senior policy researcher Jessica Jensen discusses how artificial intell', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/when-disaster-strikes-could-ai-help-qa-with-jessica.html'}, {'signal_id': '1661e5b81ca5f2ab', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Not All ‘Magic’ Mushrooms Are the Same Millions of U.S. adults use <em>Amanita muscaria</em> mushrooms. But these distinctive fungi aren’t like other psychoactive mushrooms. What do consumers and policymakers need to know about them?', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/not-all-magic-mushrooms-are-the-same.html'}, {'signal_id': '9e7a1d6837563ea8', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Mirror Life Is Theoretical. The Danger Is Anything But. With mirror life, scientists have given world leaders both the foresight and the time to address the danger. What's needed isn't alarm but action to ensure that mirror life remains just a footnote in human history&mdash;and ", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/mirror-life-is-theoretical-the-danger-is-anything-but.html'}, {'signal_id': '72a3e6dde5a2e9ab', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'As energy prices threaten inflation again, Lagarde’s European Central Bank legacy offers lessons <p>Christine Lagarde\'s European Central Bank legacy reflects strong crisis management and efforts to strengthen the euro, but a mixed record on inflation.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="htt', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/as-energy-prices-threaten-inflation-again-lagardes-european-central-bank-legacy-offers-lessons/'}, {'signal_id': 'c5f106fd0eb26daa', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Washington Tariff & Trade Letter on the US’s use of Smoot-Hawley law to impose tariffs on Canada <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-washington-tariff-trade-letter-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-washington-tariff-trade-letter-on-the-uss-use-of-smoot-hawley-law-to-impose-tariffs-on-canada/'}, {'signal_id': '8b2a0910ab390025', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in National Post on the implications of USMCA uncertainty on long-term North American supply chain security <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-national-post-on-the-im', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-national-post-on-the-implications-of-usmca-uncertainty-on-long-term-north-american-supply-chain-security/'}, {'signal_id': '5544debd93d9e27e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Reforma on how China benefits from USMCA uncertainty and fragmentation <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-reforma-on-how-china-benefits-from-usmca-uncertainty-and-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-reforma-on-how-china-benefits-from-usmca-uncertainty-and-fragmentation/'}, {'signal_id': 'd6db05d976be6e1f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Financial Review on the USMCA renegotiating process and the implications of uncertainty for the trade bloc <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-financial-review-on-t', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-financial-review-on-the-usmca-renegotiating-process-and-the-implications-of-uncertainty-for-the-trade-bloc/'}, {'signal_id': 'fb7557ba434605b2', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Barron’s on how Canada’s economy can sustain disruptions and mixed signals on trade from US <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-barrons-on-how-canadas-economy-can-s', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-barrons-on-how-canadas-economy-can-sustain-disruptions-and-mixed-signals-on-trade-from-us/'}, {'signal_id': '65c639722093fd44', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Nikoladze quoted in The Christian Science Monitor on the effectiveness of tariffs authorized by the Russia Sanctions Act of 2026 <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/nikoladze-quoted-in-the-christian-sci', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/nikoladze-quoted-in-the-christian-science-monitor-on-the-effectiveness-of-tariffs-authorized-by-the-russia-sanctions-act-of-2026/'}, {'signal_id': '0aea3c2432b0f44c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Nikoladze quoted in Washington Monthly on the Russia Sanctions Act of 2026’s implications for existing Russia-related sanctions <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/nikoladze-quoted-in-washington-monthly', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/nikoladze-quoted-in-washington-monthly-on-the-russia-sanctions-act-of-2026s-implications-for-existing-russia-related-sanctions/'}, {'signal_id': '7c343a0c3372803a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'CBDC Tracker cited in American Institute for Economic Research report on how countries are exploring the use of digital currencies <p>Explore the CBDC Tracker here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/cbdc-tracker-cited-in-american-i', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/cbdc-tracker-cited-in-american-institute-for-economic-research-report-on-how-countries-are-exploring-the-use-of-digital-currencies/'}, {'signal_id': '2321f3f198e