atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/donovan-and-ezratty-cited-in-foreign-policy-on-russias-and-chinas-material-assistance-for-irans-war-efforts/'}, {'signal_id': '526113215fd7d719', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chhangani quoted in Arabian Gulf Business Insight on the implications of Saudi Arabia’s exit from mBridge <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chhangani-quoted-in-arabian-gulf-business-insight-on-the-imp', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chhangani-quoted-in-arabian-gulf-business-insight-on-the-implications-of-saudi-arabias-exit-from-mbridge/'}, {'signal_id': 'a4f988a46237e286', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Goodwin-Groen quoted in Rzeczpospolita on the importance of modernized payment systems and digital currencies for development <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/goodwin-groen-quoted-in-rzeczpospolita-o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/goodwin-groen-quoted-in-rzeczpospolita-on-the-importance-of-modernized-payment-systems-and-digital-currencies-for-development/'}, {'signal_id': '49dffb503a71f45f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Tannebaum interviewed on Bloomberg Surveillance on US-Ukraine relations and Russian peace talks <p>Listen to the full podcast episode here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-interviewed-on-bloomberg-surveillance-on-us-ukr', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-interviewed-on-bloomberg-surveillance-on-us-ukraine-relations-and-russian-peace-talks/'}, {'signal_id': '341b1ea3a5724c2c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Libya’s maritime deal with Turkey may be the key to reunification <p>The deal, and the rise of Saddam Haftar, represent a new approach to Libya’s divided domestic politics and foreign relations.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/libyas-mari', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/libyas-maritime-deal-with-turkey-may-be-the-key-to-reunification/'}, {'signal_id': '6214ccc141678b8c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The relationship between female leadership, political freedom, and the rule of law <p>How is female leadership in public service associated with two institutional outcomes: political freedom and rule of law? Understanding the broader implications of women’s representation in lead', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/the-relationship-between-female-leadership-political-freedom-and-the-rule-law/'}, {'signal_id': 'b8e9d8132e49afe6', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukraine’s drone defenses debunk the myth of inevitable Russian victory <p>Ukraine’s emergence since 2022 as a drone superpower has made international headlines, but the role of drone-based air defenses on the battlefield has not yet received as much attention as it arguably deser', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraines-drone-defenses-debunk-the-myth-of-inevitable-russian-victory/'}, {'signal_id': 'c18fe6e50c050bd1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'France’s protests are playing into Le Pen’s hands <p>Protests have shifted France\'s national debate toward restoring order, a narrative that aligns closely with Marine Le Pen’s and the French right’s messaging.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/f', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/frances-protests-are-playing-into-le-pens-hands/'}, {'signal_id': '8f192a81cd682464', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Putin’s quest to reclaim ‘historical Russian lands’ is a recipe for endless war <p>Russian President Vladimir Putin\'s insistence that Ukraine is "historically Russian land" reveals the extent of his imperial ambitions and represents a recipe for endless war, writes Peter Dickinso', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/putins-quest-to-reclaim-historical-russian-lands-is-a-recipe-for-endless-war/'}, {'signal_id': 'cf7f77bd43401708', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Rethinking political risk in Argentina: Why the next election may matter less than investors think <p>Argentina’s next election could shake markets even without reversing Milei’s reforms.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/rethinking-political-ris', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/rethinking-political-risk-in-argentina-why-the-next-election-may-matter-less-than-investors-think/'}, {'signal_id': '24932cdefceb268a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The Board of Peace for Gaza is not a commercial enterprise. It should stop acting like one. <p>The Board of Peace is missing the infrastructure, funding, and security guarantees it needs to make progress on its mission.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blo', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/the-board-of-peace-for-gaza-is-not-a-commercial-enterprise-it-should-stop-acting-like-one/'}, {'signal_id': 'b465cd68433e191e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How Far Could the Student List Reshape Serbia? | A Debrief With Misha Glenny <p>Europe Center Resident Senior Fellow Ilva Tare speaks with Misha Glenny to discuss Serbia\'s parliamentary results. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/balkans-debr', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/balkans-debrief/how-far-could-the-student-list-reshape-serbia-a-debrief-with-misha-glenny/'}, {'signal_id': 'a7d346a295f59899', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How the Israeli election deadlock could end <p>The path ahead for either candidate in Israel\'s election to form a working coalition is uncertain. We polled our experts on what comes next. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/fast-t', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/fast-thinking-how-the-israeli-election-deadlock-could-end/'}, {'signal_id': '9bd8e6cbb265e3af', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'For Russia, Trump’s diesel deal was just the first ask <p>The rationale behind the Trump administration’s recently issued General License 135 faces a number of questions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/for-russia-trumps-diesel-deal-was-just-th', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/for-russia-trumps-diesel-deal-was-just-the-first-ask/'}, {'signal_id': '6620381792a8ec02', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'UN report: Russian attacks on Ukraine’s power grid are a ‘crime against humanity’ <p>Russia’s bombardment of Ukraine’s civilian power grid qualifies as a crime against humanity, according to a new report by the UN’s Independent International Commission of Inquiry on Ukraine, writ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/un-report-russian-attacks-on-ukraines-power-grid-are-a-crime-against-humanity/'}, {'signal_id': 'd2320ec53d07edb6', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'High oil prices have several Latin American governments feeling the financial pressure <p>Three charts show why oil prices that exceed 2026 budget assumptions matter for both importers and exporters.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/high-oil-pri', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/high-oil-prices-have-several-latin-american-governments-feeling-the-financial-pressure/'}, {'signal_id': '24e997d5aae2ae7b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'European infrastructure is vulnerable as Putin escalates Russia’s hybrid war <p>Putin is currently looking to exploit Europe’s vulnerabilities as he seeks ways to isolate Ukraine and cut off Kyiv’s European aid lifeline. Civilian infrastructure may be one of the continent’s weake', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/european-infrastructure-is-vulnerable-as-putin-escalates-russias-hybrid-war/'}, {'signal_id': '204bfadfb879faaf', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Why France and Turkey are giving defense cooperation another go <p>France and Turkey still disagree on plenty, but Europe’s changing security environment is giving them stronger reasons to cooperate.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/turkeysource/fran', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/turkeysource/france-and-turkey-sign-2026-defense-roadmap/'}, {'signal_id': '616304587ab0c748', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The United States needs an energy policy investors can bank on <p>Unlocking long-term private investment in US energy infrastructure requires a federal policy framework driven by performance, not political preference.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/energysource/the-united-states-needs-an-energy-policy-investors-can-bank-on/'}, {'signal_id': '6852301af360f4c6', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Any means necessary: Are courts safe in the digital age? <p>Reports are on the rise of hacks at federal courts in the United States, putting sensitive data, such as informants' identities, at risk. In litigation involving spyware, even more sensitive data is at risk. What protect", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/any-means-necessary-are-courts-safe-in-the-digital-age/'}, {'signal_id': '774544594e3a0d7c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Experts react: Serbia’s Vučić is out and the student-led movement is in. What comes next? <p>Serbia’s student-led opposition just ended Vučić’s fourteen years at the helm. Atlantic Council experts assess what comes next.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/di', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/experts-react-serbias-vucic-is-out-and-the-student-led-movement-is-in-what-comes-next/'}, {'signal_id': '830b870cf2cf7380', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Some reasons for hope in Israel’s sharply divided election <p>Regardless of the outcome, the end of campaigning could open chances for diplomacy that were previously closed. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/some-reasons-for-hope-in-israels-shar', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/some-reasons-for-hope-in-israels-sharply-divided-election/'}, {'signal_id': 'f3105e55b72fcd0e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Should Beijing be pushed to let the renminbi rise? <p>Can currency diplomacy address the global imbalances that have featured on both the Group of 7 and Group of Twenty agendas this year? And can the US and the EU finally align their strategies to tackle China's overcapacity? Bra", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/podcast/should-beijing-be-pushed-to-let-the-renminbi-rise/'}, {'signal_id': 'e8acc90d9099a0a0', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Pakistan’s changing development assistance landscape: Manifestations, implications, and opportunities <p>Pakistan’s development assistance landscape is undergoing a major structural shift. Western bilateral aid is declining, multilateral development bank (MDB) financing is increa', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/pakistans-changing-development-assistance-landscape-manifestations-implications-and-opportunities/'}, {'signal_id': '9f36eae9d80182b8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Bangladesh’s changing development assistance landscape: Manifestations, implications, and opportunities <p>Bangladesh is absorbing one of the 