uencing-de-doll', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4/'}, {'signal_id': '91b460ea962e0dd5', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'CBDC Tracker cited in Citi report, The Connective Tissue of Digital Finance: Interoperability, Programmability, and the Path to Institutional Scale. <p>Read the article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/the-cbdc-tracker-cited', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/the-cbdc-tracker-cited-in-coindesk-on-the-number-of-countries-actively-testing-or-developing-cbdcs-2/'}, {'signal_id': 'f753bcda01e1ee02', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chhangani cited in Forbes article on Saudi Arabia’s withdrawal from the mBridge CBDC platform. <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-3/'}, {'signal_id': 'd68ead9a82c828af', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'De Kruijf cited in National Interest article on the Trump administration’s policy toward the International Criminal Court (ICC) <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-bloomberg-article-o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-bloomberg-article-on-the-impact-of-usmca-uncertainty-on-supply-chains-2/'}, {'signal_id': '815479d013ed2eca', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Trump will define his legacy through Russia—one way or the other <p>The US president inherited Russia’s war on Ukraine, but he will own the consequences of how it ends.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/trump-will-define-his', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/trump-will-define-his-legacy-through-russia-one-way-or-the-other/'}, {'signal_id': '7c96f28b319b0b20', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukrainians are not fighting for Zelenskyy. They are fighting for national survival. <p>Trump and Putin both seem to think that removing Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy would set the stage for a Kremlin-friendly peace deal, but most Ukrainians see the war as a fight for na', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukrainians-are-not-fighting-for-zelenskyy-they-are-fighting-for-survival/'}, {'signal_id': 'e1aa97b5e500a1d3', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The new Middle East is modular <p>In the Middle East today, states are aligning issue by issue, not choosing sides. They cooperate in one area and compete in the next. This modular alignment is shaping the region, even as it manages the shocks of war and energy-market volatility.', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/the-big-story/the-new-middle-east-is-modular/'}, {'signal_id': '031868c41e60b35a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in The Sun on potential attacks on undersea infrastructure <p>On October 17, Elisabeth Braw was interviewed in The Sun to discuss the threat of attacks on undersea cables and pipelines.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategorized/braw-in-the-sun-on', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategorized/braw-in-the-sun-on-potential-attacks-on-undersea-infrastructure/'}, {'signal_id': '4c846462d1991272', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The withdrawal of the US-led coalition is a loss for Iraq’s sovereignty <p>The government secured the withdrawal of foreign partners before securing obedience from armed factions. That leaves Baghdad with less leverage against Iran’s allies in Iraq.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/the-withdrawal-of-the-us-led-coalition-is-a-loss-for-iraqs-sovereignty/'}, {'signal_id': 'a4b90adb56fe2f62', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Washington should stop expecting the Gulf to speak with one voice <p>Gulf states are emerging from the Iran war with different conclusions about how to protect themselves and deal with Tehran.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/washington-should-s', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/washington-should-stop-expecting-the-gulf-to-speak-with-one-voice/'}, {'signal_id': 'de76972bfc933bc8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Moldova’s fight against Kremlin interference faces Gagauzia election test <p>Moldova’s democratic resilience faces a revealing litmus test on November 15, when autonomous Gagauzia elects a new governor and People’s Assembly amid concerns over Kremlin interference, write Laurențiu', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/moldovas-fight-against-kremlin-interference-faces-gagauzia-election-test/'}, {'signal_id': 'af88f29163bd1dfa', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Russian attacks on Ukrainian civilians may have a domestic dimension <p>Russia's escalating bombing campaign against civilian targets across Ukraine aims to make much of the country unlivable while also serving a propaganda purpose for the Kremlin on the home front, write Syrus S", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/russian-attacks-on-ukrainian-civilians-may-have-a-domestic-dimension/'}, {'signal_id': 'e15af6013a810c50', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What a Lula or Bolsonaro victory would mean for Brazil and the world <p>Brazil’s presidential runoff could open a narrow window for closer US-Brazil cooperation on trade, security, and critical minerals.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-a-l', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-a-lula-or-bolsonaro-victory-would-mean-for-brazil-and-the-world/'}, {'signal_id': '783a71a7dac154ac', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Sean Welch quoted in National Defense Magazine on the Marine Corps’ modernization plan <p>On October 21, Forward Defense nonresident senior fellow Sean Welch was quoted in a National Defense Magazine article on the Ground Combat Element 2040 Fiscal Year 2026. Welch argued that th', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/sean-welch-quoted-in-national-defense-magazine-on-the-marine-corps-modernization-plan/'}, {'signal_id': '036e16672b256b72', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Six military freezers went bad in August. Was it a cyber attack? After food spoiled at commissaries, Pentagon investigators are looking at similar incidents in France.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/threats/2026/10/pentagon-investigates-suspected-cyberattack-behind-military-freezer-failures/416929/'}, {'signal_id': '3c856e89d66739b9', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Army pilots are trying virtual reality to stay more alert in flight The 101st Combat Aviation Brigade is testing the NeuroTrainer as a possible readiness tool for their aviators.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/technology/2026/10/army-pilots-are-trying-virtual-reality-stay-more-alert-flight/416915/'}, {'signal_id': 'bd61e8e87f2fc7c7', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Can inertial navigation make ground-robot swarms real? Two startups are equipping small wheeled robots with a GPS-free nav package.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/defense-systems/2026/10/inertial-navigation-ground-robot-swarms/416914/'}, {'signal_id': 'bc052e87ce858512', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Defense Business Brief: Tech at the edge; PACFLEET talks cyber; and more', 'url': 'https://www.defe